; fas9_history.scr - facit script of step 9.14 (F9.10, the solids' history): ACSH_HISTORY_CLASS and its nodes, made by AutoCAD 2025's
; own core. Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_history.scr
; It starts from acad.dwt (a new empty drawing) and uses plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (the core has none). SOLIDHIST 1 comes first:
; every solid made after it carries a history (ACSH_HISTORY_CLASS owned by the solid, the ACAD_EVALUATION_GRAPH the history owns, one
; node object per operation). Edges and faces are picked by a point on them in the south-west isometric view (the core resolves a
; typed point to the edge), the profiles of a window selection in the plan view after ZOOM Extents (an object outside the view is
; not selectable in the core); a window must have the object whole inside it.
;
; Files (acad_<version>_dxf_<theme>[_<change>][_bin].dxf, 2000 ... 2018; the core cannot save R13/R14; 2000 and 2004 have no history,
; AutoCAD drops it there):
;   history_primitives                   BOX 20x15x20, SPHERE r12, CYLINDER r10 h25, CONE r12 h30, TORUS 15/4, WEDGE 25x20x20, PYRAMID
;                                        5 sides r15 h25 (all with non-default sizes), a frustum CONE r12 top 5, an elliptical CYLINDER
;                                        (axes 4 and 10), a PYRAMID of 6 sides with a top radius: the primitives' own subclasses
;   history_primitives rotated           the box turned 30 degrees about the X axis (ROTATE3D): its node's 40 ... 55 change
;   history_primitives moved             the box moved by (10, 5) (MOVE)
;   history_primitives mirrored          the box mirrored in the plane y = -10 (MIRROR3D)
;   history_profiles                     a rectangle extruded (profile as a bit stream), a region extruded with a 10 degree taper (profile as SAT
;                                        lines), a circle extruded along a path and swept (two source geometries: profile and path), a
;                                        REVOLVE of 270 degrees, three LOFTs: cross sections only, with two guide curves, with a path
;   history_boolean                      three pairs of solids, not yet combined
;   history_boolean applied              UNION, SUBTRACT and INTERSECT of them (ACSH_BOOLEAN_CLASS operation 0, 2 and 1)
;   history_edges                        two boxes
;   history_edges filleted               a FILLETEDGE of three edges of the first (radius 2): ACSH_FILLET_CLASS with three edges
;   history_edges chamfered              a CHAMFEREDGE of two edges of the second (distances 2 and 3): ACSH_CHAMFER_CLASS
;   history_brep                         a box that BREP has made a boundary representation of, united with another box: ACSH_BREP_CLASS
;
; What the core cannot do, and what is therefore "ej testat" (plan 2026-10-27-fas-9-typer.md, F9.10): changing a primitive's size through
; grips or the properties palette (the core has neither: only the commands above change a solid), SOLIDEDIT and PRESSPULL (they pick
; faces on the screen: PRESSPULL does not take a point on a face here), CHAMFER/FILLET of faces, a SWEEP or LOFT with twist and
; draft options set through the dialog, R13/R14.
